From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Save states: no GC while the Lua state is restored

eris rebuilds function prototypes and links them to their parent without
GC write barriers. An incremental GC step during the restore (RetroArch
saves an undo state right before every load, which leaves the collector
mid-cycle) could sweep a child prototype while it was still being filled
in: use after free in u_proto, "malloc(): unaligned tcache chunk
detected", RetroArch killed. Found with AddressSanitizer and a libretro
test host (save, undo save, load). The collector is stopped for the
restore and restarted afterwards.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/source/vm.cpp
+++ b/source/vm.cpp
@@ -1518,7 +1518,18 @@
 	lua_getfield(_luaState, -1, "restore_all");
 	lua_pushlstring(_luaState, src, len);
 
-	if (lua_pcall(_luaState, 1, 0, 0) != 0) {
+	// nuubOS: eris links the objects it rebuilds (child function
+	// prototypes, constants, names) without GC write barriers, so an
+	// incremental GC step during the restore could free a prototype still
+	// being filled in (heap corruption, "malloc(): unaligned tcache chunk").
+	// No collection while the state is restored.
+	int gcRunning = lua_gc(_luaState, LUA_GCISRUNNING, 0);
+	lua_gc(_luaState, LUA_GCSTOP, 0);
+	int status = lua_pcall(_luaState, 1, 0, 0);
+	if (gcRunning)
+		lua_gc(_luaState, LUA_GCRESTART, 0);
+
+	if (status != 0) {
 		std::string e = lua_tostring(_luaState, -1);
 		fprintf(stderr, "[fake08] Lua state not restored: %s\n", e.c_str());
 		lua_pop(_luaState, 2);
